cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'Pulse: a container-aware music player for every framework'
message: 'If you use Pulse in research or published work, please cite it as below.'
type: software
authors:
  - alias: YamadaBlog
repository-code: 'https://github.com/YamadaBlog/pulse-player'
url: 'https://yamadablog.github.io/pulse-player/'
abstract: >-
  Pulse is a drop-in music player for the web, shipped as standard Custom
  Elements with typed bindings for Vue, React and Svelte. A framework-agnostic
  TypeScript engine drives playback, the Media Session API and a Web Audio
  visualiser; the Lit renderer adapts to its container with CSS container
  queries, from a full card down to a round disc.
keywords:
  - music-player
  - audio
  - web-components
  - custom-elements
  - lit
  - vue
  - react
  - svelte
  - typescript
license: MIT
version: 3.0.0
